{"availability":"available","full":"JohnImril/diablo_web","name":"diablo_web","description":"Diablo-like browser client with React, TypeScript, Vite, WebAssembly runtime, canvas rendering, browser storage, and static deployment","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":44,"forks":9,"created":"2024-08-25T17:47:02Z","updated":"2026-10-09T00:27:01Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://johnimril.github.io/diablo_web/","topics":["browser-game","canvas","game","react","typescript","vite","wasm","webassembly"],"demo":"https://johnimril.github.io/diablo_web/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:56:55.798Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:56:55.798Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:56:55.798Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:49.269Z","stars":38,"forks":8},{"at":"2026-10-09T08:56:55.798Z","stars":44,"forks":9}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Diablo Web is a browser-based Diablo / Diablo-like experience built with Vite, React, TypeScript, and WebAssembly. The project modernizes earlier browser work around DiabloWeb and devilution-based WebAssembly builds, with a cleaner frontend structure, current Node.js compatibility, browser storage support, and a deployment flow that targets static hosting.","This repository is the main browser client. It loads the game engine through WebAssembly, manages game data in the browser, renders to canvas, and wraps the runtime in a Vite + React application.","The project started from work around DiabloWeb by d07RiV and the devilution community. An intermediate Node.js 22-compatible fork is available at JohnImril/diabloweb-beta. Diablo Web then rebuilt the client shell around Vite and TypeScript while keeping the WebAssembly engine path central to the runtime."],"features":["Browser-based Diablo / Diablo-like runtime using WebAssembly.","Vite-powered development and static production builds.","TypeScript application shell with React UI components.","Node.j